T*
(* Process Definition: An active program in execution \(including Program Counter, CPU) Tj
T*
(registers, Stack, Heap, Data, and Text sections\).) Tj
T*
(* Process Control Block \(PCB\): The data structure maintaining process state: Process) Tj
T*
(ID \(PID\), Program Counter, CPU Registers, CPU Scheduling Information,) Tj
T*
(Memory-Management Info, I/O Status & Open File Descriptors.) Tj
T*
(* 5-State Process Model: New -> Ready \(in memory waiting for CPU\) -> Running) Tj
T*
(\(instructions executing\) -> Waiting/Blocked \(waiting for I/O or event\) -> Terminated.) Tj
T*
(* Context Switching: The mechanism of saving the state of the currently running) Tj
T*
(process to its PCB and loading the saved state of another ready process into CPU) Tj
