T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Optimization Goals: Maximize CPU Utilization and Throughput; Minimize Turnaround) Tj
T*
(Time \(TAT = Completion - Arrival\), Waiting Time \(WT = TAT - Burst Time\), and Response) Tj
T*
(Time.) Tj
T*
(* Core Scheduling Algorithms:) Tj
T*
(- 1. First-Come First-Served \(FCFS\): Non-preemptive. Suffers from Convoy Effect \(short) Tj
T*
(processes stuck behind a long CPU-bound process\).) Tj
T*
(- 2. Shortest Job First \(SJF\) / Shortest Remaining Time First \(SRTF\): Provably optimal) Tj
T*
(average waiting time. Preemptive variant is SRTF. Suffers from potential starvation of) Tj
T*
(long processes.) Tj
T*
(- 3. Round Robin \(RR\): Preemptive. Each process gets a fixed time quantum q. If burst >) Tj
T*
(q, process is preempted and placed at tail of ready queue. Fair, interactive.) Tj
T*
(- 4. Priority Scheduling: CPU assigned to highest priority process. Starvation prevented) Tj
T*
(via Aging \(gradually increasing priority of waiting processes\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
