(>> 3.4 Inter-Process Synchronization and Deadlock Theory) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Race Condition: A concurrency flaw where output depends critically on the) Tj
T*
(non-deterministic execution sequence or interleaving of competing threads.) Tj
T*
(* Critical Section Problem: Code segment accessing shared resources. Solutions must) Tj
T*
(satisfy: Mutual Exclusion, Progress, and Bounded Waiting.) Tj
T*
(* Semaphores: Synchronization primitive with atomic operations wait\(\) \(P\) and) Tj
T*
(signal\(\) \(V\). Binary Semaphore \(Mutex\) takes values 0 and 1; Counting Semaphore) Tj
T*
(manages multiple resource instances.) Tj
T*
(* Deadlock: A permanent blocking condition where every process in a set waits for a) Tj
T*
(resource held by another process in the set.) Tj
T*
(* The 4 Coffman Necessary Conditions for Deadlock:) Tj
T*
(- 1. Mutual Exclusion: At least one resource held in non-shareable mode.) Tj
T*
(- 2. Hold and Wait: Process holding resources requests additional resources.) Tj
T*
(- 3. No Preemption: Resources cannot be forcibly confiscated from a process.) Tj
T*
(- 4. Circular Wait: A closed loop chain of processes where P_i waits for resource held) Tj
T*
(by P_\(i+1\).) Tj
T*
(* Deadlock Handling: Deadlock Prevention, Deadlock Avoidance \(Banker''s Algorithm for) Tj
T*
(safe states\), Deadlock Detection and Recovery.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
