(* Physical vs Logical Address: Logical address generated by CPU; translated into) Tj
T*
(Physical Address in DRAM by Memory Management Unit \(MMU\).) Tj
T*
(* Paging Architecture: Logical memory divided into fixed-size blocks called Pages;) Tj
T*
(physical memory divided into equal-sized blocks called Frames. Page Table maps Page) Tj
T*
(Number to Frame Number.) Tj
T*
(* Translation Lookaside Buffer \(TLB\): High-speed associative hardware cache storing) Tj
T*
(recently used Page-to-Frame mappings to accelerate address translation.) Tj
T*
(* Virtual Memory: Allows execution of processes not completely loaded in physical RAM) Tj
T*
(using Demand Paging.) Tj
T*
(* Page Replacement Algorithms \(executed upon Page Fault when all RAM frames are) Tj
T*
(occupied\):) Tj
T*
(- FIFO \(First-In, First-Out\): Suffers from Belady''s Anomaly \(more frames can produce) Tj
T*
(more page faults\).) Tj
T*
(- LRU \(Least Recently Used\): Replaces page that has not been referenced for longest) Tj
T*
(duration. Optimal practical algorithm.) Tj
T*
(- Optimal \(OPT\): Replaces page that will not be used for longest future duration) Tj
T*
(\(theoretical benchmark\).) Tj
