([PROBLEM 1: Comparative CPU Scheduling Analysis: FCFS vs Round Robin]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Statement: Three processes arrive at time 0 with the following CPU burst times:) Tj
T*
(P1 = 24 ms, P2 = 3 ms, P3 = 3 ms. Compare First-Come First-Served \(FCFS\) and Round Robin) Tj
T*
(\(RR with time quantum q = 4 ms\) in terms of: \(1\) Gantt Chart, \(2\) Turnaround Time, and) Tj
T*
(\(3\) Average Waiting Time.) Tj
T*
(Mathematical Derivation & Evaluation:) Tj
T*
(* 1. FCFS Scheduling Execution:) Tj
T*
(- Gantt Chart: [ P1: 0 to 24 ] [ P2: 24 to 27 ] [ P3: 27 to 30 ].) Tj
T*
(- Completion Times: P1 = 24, P2 = 27, P3 = 30.) Tj
T*
(- Waiting Times: P1 = 0 ms, P2 = 24 ms, P3 = 27 ms.) Tj
T*
(- Average Waiting Time \(FCFS\) = \(0 + 24 + 27\) / 3 = 51 / 3 = 17.0 ms.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Round Robin Scheduling Execution \(q = 4 ms\):) Tj
T*
(- Gantt Chart: [ P1: 0 to 4 ] [ P2: 4 to 7 ] [ P3: 7 to 10 ] [ P1: 10 to 30 ].) Tj
T*
(- Note: P2 finishes at t = 7; P3 finishes at t = 10; P1 resumes at t = 10 and finishes) Tj
T*
(remaining 20 ms at t = 30.) Tj
T*
(- Completion Times: P1 = 30, P2 = 7, P3 = 10.) Tj
T*
(- Waiting Times: P1 = \(0\) + \(10 - 4\) = 6 ms; P2 = 4 ms; P3 = 7 ms.) Tj
T*
(- Average Waiting Time \(RR\) = \(6 + 4 + 7\) / 3 = 17 / 3 = 5.67 ms.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Engineering Conclusion: Round Robin drastically slashes average waiting time) Tj
T*
(from 17.0 ms to 5.67 ms \(a 3x improvement\) by eliminating the convoy effect.) Tj
T*
