([PROBLEM 4: Logical-to-Physical Address Translation in Paging]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Statement: A 32-bit computing system uses paging with 4 KB \(2^12 bytes\) page) Tj
T*
(size. A process generates logical address 0x0002A3F4. If Page Table entry for Page) Tj
T*
(0x0002A holds Frame Number 0x0010B, determine the exact physical DRAM address.) Tj
T*
(Mathematical Derivation:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Address Bit Division: Page Size = 4 KB = 2^12 bytes -> Offset occupies 12 bits) Tj
T*
(\(3 hex digits\). Remaining 20 bits \(5 hex digits\) represent Page Number.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Decompose Logical Address 0x0002A3F4:) Tj
T*
(- Page Number \(p\) = 0x0002A.) Tj
T*
(- Offset \(d\) = 0x3F4.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Frame Lookup: Page Table indicates Frame Number \(f\) = 0x0010B.) Tj
T*
(* 4. Form Physical Address: Physical Address = \(Frame Number << 12\) | Offset =) Tj
T*
(0x0010B000 + 0x3F4 = 0x0010B3F4.) Tj
T*
